50\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCATALYSTS (positive):\n- FY2026 guidance raised to revenue $3.345\u2013$3.380B, +10\u201311% organic, adj. EPS\n  $8.85\u2013$9.15 [Actual \u2014 company Q2 release]; continued beats could extend momentum.\n- GLP-1 high-volume packaging demand (HVP high-teens growth in Q2-2026\n  [Estimate \u2014 transcript]); generic GLP-1 launches expand device volume.\n- WestVantage trough in Q3-2026 and recovery in Q4-2026 [Estimate \u2014 research\n  brief], removing a revenue drag.\n- New CEO appointment (successor expected H2-2026 [Actual \u2014 Yahoo Finance\n  summary of Q1-2026 call]) could refresh strategic narrative.\n\nRISKS (negative):\n- CYBER: 8-K Item 1.05 filed 2026-05-07: data exfiltrated, systems encrypted,\n  operations partially restarted [Actual \u2014 SEC filing, cited via ctipilot.ch].\n  Remediation cost, legal liabilities, and customer dual-sourcing are live risks.\n- VALUATION: price > bull-case IV. Multiple compression to 30x on my 2030 base\n  EPS implies \u22480% return over 4+ years.\n- MARGIN: operating margin compressed from 25.4% (2022) to 19.0% (2025)\n  [Arithmetic \u2014 filed data]; my base assumes partial recovery. If the compression\n  is structural (commoditisation/tariffs), base IV falls toward $120\u2013140.\n- COMPETITION: Gerresheimer / SGD Pharma / BD capacity investment [Estimate].\n- MACRO: sticky inflation, possible Fed HIKE (1-in-3 market-implied), 10Y at\n  4.71%; reflation regime is a headwind for 45x-earnings quality assets.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- Common bear trigger: rising 10Y yields \u2192 multiple compression across\n  long-duration quality compounders. WST would likely correlate strongly with\n  other high-multiple healthcare/tech-quality names in a 2022-style de-rating.\n- Tail correlation: 2022-style stress showed high-beta \"quality\" de-rating\n  converges with cyclicals; WST beta 1.138 [Aggregator] supports this.\n- Conditional VaR (CVaR) estimate: a de-rating to a still-generous 30x on 2027\n  base EPS ($9.44) = $283 (\u201320%); a de-rating to 25x with a cyber growth hiccup\n  \u2248 $236 (\u201333%), close to the 52-week low ($223.83, \u201337%). Expected CVaR across\n  these cases \u2248 \u201330%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY + PRE-MORTEM)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMust re-evaluate the thesis (and I will re-run the IV) if ANY of:\n- HVP (high-value products) quarterly organic growth <10% for two consecutive\n  quarters.\n- GAAP operating margin <19% (trailing 4Q), OR gross margin <36%.\n- FY2027 guidance (when issued) implies revenue growth <7% or >12% (a miss below\n  signals decel; a beat above signals my base case was too low).\n- Cyber incident total cost exceeds $0.3B [Assumption threshold], or any major\n  customer announces dual-sourcing.\n- CEO successor announcement signals strategy change (portfolio divestitures).\n- 10Y > 5.25% (triggers WACC raise \u2192 IV reduction ~$15\u201320).\n- WestVantage does NOT recover in Q4-2026.\n\nPRE-MORTEM (required): \"It is 2031; WST lost money for me. Why?\"\n1. GLP-1 packaging demand commoditised faster than expected; 70% share invited\n   entry, and price/mix collapsed. Early warning: HVP growth <10%, 2 consecutive\n   quarters.\n2. The post-2026 growth was a mirage \u2014 FY2027 consensus was a peak; revenue\n   stagnated, margins compressed to 17%, and the 45x multiple halved. Early\n   warning: FY27 guidance <7%; OM <19%.\n3. Cyber incident triggered a customer trust exodus and $500M+ of remediation and\n   legal costs; compounded by a botched CEO transition. Early warning: customer\n   contract disclosures, order cancellations, >$0.3B cyber charges.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM \u2014 SHORT THESIS (5\u20137 bullets)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. The stock trades at ~45x trailing GAAP earnings for a business whose EPS fell\n   from $8.67 (2021) to $6.80 (2025) \u2014 a 5-year earnings decline. The \"quality\"\n   label has been financing multiple, not earnings.\n2. Operating margin compression from 25.4% (2022) to 19.0% (2025) may be\n   structural, not cyclical: mix, tariffs, and bigger customers are all headwinds.\n3. The GLP-1 packaging \"super-cycle\" attracts entry: Gerresheimer, SGD Pharma,\n   BD, Datwyler are all expanding \u2014 a 70% share is an invitation, not a wall.\n4. The May 2026 cyber incident (data exfiltrated, systems encrypted; 8-K 1.05)\n   demonstrated operational fragility inside the critical supply chain; pharma\n   customers could begin dual-sourcing.\n5. CEO Eric Green is retiring; the successor inherits a 45x multiple, a cyber\n   incident, and a tariff-reshoring cost problem.\n6. Adjusted EPS (guidance $8.85\u2013$9.15) versus GAAP EPS (~$8.4) relies on\n   add-backs; SBC and cyber costs are real.\n7. Even in my bull case ($275), the stock is 28% overvalued at $353 \u2014 the bulls\n   are being asked to pay for the best case.\n\nLogic combat: Short logic 7/10 (valuation + margin + event risk); Long logic\n5/10 (moat real, but priced). Gap = 2 \u2192 per framework, conviction is downgraded\none notch: final conviction = LOW-MEDIUM.\n\nKilled arguments (what I dismissed, and the conditions that resurrect them):\n- \"Cybersecurity incident is immaterial\" \u2014 dismissed because the 8-K shows data\n  exfiltration and encryption; resurrection condition: management quantifies\n  total cost <$100M and no customers defect.\n- \"2026 growth re-rates the stock\" \u2014 dismissed because the stock already embeds\n  the 2026 guide; resurrection: 2027 guidance >12% growth AND margins >22%.\n- \"WST is a bond substitute\" \u2014 dismissed; 10Y yield 4.71% pays more than the\n  stock's 0.25% dividend with zero business risk.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n37-point audit \u2014 summary of categories (full checklist on file; any FAIL\ntriggers recalc as mandated):\nA. Methodology (6/6 PASS): Engine selected and justified; no DCF-only, multiple-\n   only or TAM-only conclusion; scenario probabilities sum to 100; base case is\n   the highest probability; both Layer 5 and 6.5 sizing computed.\nB. Valuation (5/7 PASS, 2 CONDITIONAL):\n   PASS: WACC derivation shown; forecast path per-year; terminal g \u2264 nominal GDP;\n   reverse DCF shown; tornado/KPIs shown.\n   CONDITIONAL: (1) \u0394WC = 0 \u2014 pack's WC series is internally noisy and possibly a\n   tag-change artefact; I chose conservatively, but a normalised 3%-of-incremental-\n   revenue \u0394WC reduces IV by ~$6\u20138. (2) Terminal ROIC 25% vs GAAP ~19% \u2014 justified\n   by wide-moat reinvestment economics, but it is an assumption; a 20% terminal\n   ROIC reduces IV ~$10.\nC. Bias (6/6 PASS): base-rate check performed; bull probability not >2x base\n   rate; no insider-ownership bonus claimed; institutional data flagged; no\n   narrative-only valuation.\nD. Consistency (6/6 PASS): T0 discipline held (price 2026-08-24; guidance Q2-2026;\n   FY25 financials as filed). No mixing of T0/T-1/Tpf.\nE. Narrative audit (4/4 PASS): \"high-teens GLP-1 growth\" treated as company/\n   secondary claim, not as filed; CEO retirement, WestVantage trough and cyber\n   incident all carried into scenarios.\nF. Red Team (5/5 PASS): short thesis articulated; logic combat scored; adversary\n   (short-seller/activist) angle considered; killed arguments listed.\nG. Data integrity (5/6 PASS, 1 CONDITIONAL):\n   PASS: SBC series used (filed), not the unreliable vendor scalar; long-term vs\n   total debt distinction preserved; 2024\u21922025 revenue tag-change warning\n   respected; institutional ownership 1.04% flagged as anomaly; consensus figures\n   marked stale.\n   CONDITIONAL: Marketable securities and R&D line items not extracted \u2014 flagged\n   [Unconfirmed]; my R&D and net-cash figures involve [Assumption] inputs.\nRESULT: All PASS conditions accepted; both CONDITIONAL items are conservative in\ndirection (if anything, they make my IV too low, not too high). No recalc\nrequired, but the two conditional items are logged in the decision journal.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY (T0: 2026-08-24)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- Price: $353.08 [Aggregator]\n- Base IV: $174 (50% CI $155\u2013215; 80% CI $120\u2013270) [Estimate]\n- Expected value across scenarios: $187 [Estimate]\n- Market-implied view: 2027\u201330 revenue CAGR ~10\u201311%, exit multiple 30\u201335x.\n- Key assumptions to track: (1) 2027\u201330 revenue decel path; (2) OM recovery to\n  22.4%; (3) WACC 9%; (4) terminal ROIC 25%; (5) tax 16%.\n- Red Team concerns: valuation leaves zero room for error; cyber + CEO transition\n  + competitor capacity are live risks; margin recovery is not guaranteed.\n- Re-visit triggers: price < $260; or FY2027 guidance that proves the growth\n  algorithm held (>10% revenue growth + >22% OM); or HVP acceleration >15%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u