n1.5-2. Deviation from base rate: Our model expects high-single-digit growth and margin expansion beyond FY2026. Deviating upward from base rate is justified by: (a) HVP components growth of 18\u201319% with mix >49% of total revenue; (b) regulatory re-qualification lock-in (2\u20133 year switching costs); (c) GLP-1 elastomer demand is a structural volume adder, not a one-timer. [Actual/Estimate]\n\n1.5-3. Base-rate shock check: Our success probability (~70% for sustained double-digit growth) is within 1.5x of comparable base rates. No red flag.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\n2-1. Business understanding: WST supplies the primary packaging (elastomeric stoppers, vials, syringes) and delivery devices for injectable medicines. Its products sit directly inside regulated drug products; any change requires customer regulatory re-validation. Understandability: High.\n\n2-2. Moat assessment (0\u20133 per moat type)\nIntangible assets: 3 | Switching costs: 3 | Network effects: 1 | Cost advantage: 2 | Economies of scale: 3 | Regulatory barriers: 3 | Data moat: 1 \u2192 Total: 16/21 = Fortress. Direction: Widening (HVP mix 49%, GLP-1 share gains, Annex-1 upgrade tailwind [Actual \u2013 management call]).\n\n2-3. Lynch classification: Fast Grower (HVP > 15% organic). Checkpoints: high HVP mix, pricing power, no single-customer concentration disclosed. Risk: growth normalizes post-2027.\n\n2-4. Financial strength scorecard\n- Revenue CAGR 3-yr (FY22\u2013FY25): +2.1% [Arithmetic] (distorted by COVID normalizing); 5-yr: +7.4% [Arithmetic]; 10-yr: +8.2% [Arithmetic]\n- Latest opera